# No auto-commit (local work)

When working in this repo locally, **do not commit or push** unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do not

- Commit after finishing a task, fix, or feature
- Push to remote "to save work" or update a PR branch
- Offer to commit proactively at the end of a response
- Amend, rebase, or create branches for git housekeeping unless requested

## Do

- Make file edits and leave changes unstaged / uncommitted
- Tell the user what changed and that they can commit when ready
- Run `git status` or `git diff` when useful for debugging or summarizing — read-only is fine
- Commit **only** when the user clearly asks (e.g. "commit this", "check in the plan", "push to level_gen")

## If unclear

Ask once: "Want me to commit these changes?" — default is **no commit**.
